{
  "opening": "This release introduces significant enhancements to the datetime parsing capabilities, including support for C standard format codes and flexible timezone handling. It also expands the parser's robustness by allowing hyphens in field names and grouping characters in decimal formats.",
  "requirements": [
    {
      "id": "m18",
      "text": "The Parser must correctly parse datetimes using C standard format codes, defaulting missing years to the current year when day or month fields are present. Single-digit days and months must be handled flexibly, and timezone offsets should be parsed with greater flexibility while shielding Python 2 from incompatible features."
    },
    {
      "id": "m20",
      "text": "The public API must expose FixedTzOffset and RepeatedNameError as distinct exception types or classes available for import. The date_convert and extract_format functions must continue to operate correctly within the refactored module structure without changing their external signatures."
    },
    {
      "id": "m22",
      "text": "The Parser class must expose a 'format' property that returns the original format string used to create the instance. The parse method must remain functional and return Result objects consistent with previous behavior."
    },
    {
      "id": "m24",
      "text": "The datetime parser must accept various numbers of digits after the comma for the %f microsecond format specifier, rather than strictly requiring six digits."
    },
    {
      "id": "m26",
      "text": "The Parser must allow hyphen-minus characters within field names in the format specification string. The extract_format function must correctly identify and process these hyphenated field names."
    },
    {
      "id": "m33",
      "text": "The Parser must support grouping characters (commas or underscores) in decimal format strings for numeric parsing. These grouping characters should be ignored during extraction, allowing inputs like '1_000' or '1,000' to parse correctly into integer values."
    }
  ],
  "closing": "Please ensure all new parsing behaviors are validated against edge cases, particularly regarding timezone offsets and flexible digit counts. Verify that existing tests pass and that the public interface remains stable for downstream consumers."
}
